---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy' },
];
const updated = 'May 28, 2026';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy : Fortify AI by i-NETT"
  description="Privacy policy covering CCPA, GDPR, and PIPEDA obligations. How i-NETT collects, uses, retains, and protects information about visitors and customers of i-nett.ai."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  pageHeading="Privacy Policy"
  pageLead={`Last updated ${updated}. This policy explains how i-NETT collects, uses, and protects information about visitors and customers of i-nett.ai. Built to satisfy CCPA, GDPR, and PIPEDA obligations.`}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  hideFinalCta={true}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container-narrow legal">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        i-NETT (referred to here as &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;)
        operates the website at <a href="https://i-nett.ai">i-nett.ai</a> and the Fortify AI
        managed AI offering. Our parent organization site is at
        <a href={SITE.parentUrl}>i-nett.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect two categories of information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you provide.</strong> When you submit a form, request a consultation,
          subscribe to the podcast, or contact us, you may provide your name, business email,
          phone number, firm name, role, and any message content you send.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> When you visit the site, our servers
          and analytics tools collect standard log information such as IP address, browser type,
          referring URL, pages visited, and timestamps. We use this to operate, secure, and
          improve the site.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not sell personal information.</li>
        <li>We do not share personal information with third parties for their independent marketing purposes.</li>
        <li>We do not use customer data submitted through Fortify AI deployments to train AI models.</li>
        <li>We do not share customer data across Fortify AI customers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your inquiries and provide the services you request.</li>
        <li>To operate, secure, and improve i-nett.ai.</li>
        <li>To send you transactional or service messages related to a Fortify AI engagement or your inquiry.</li>
        <li>To comply with legal obligations, enforce our terms, and protect our rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Legal bases (GDPR)</h2>
      <p>
        For visitors and customers in the European Economic Area and United Kingdom, we process
        personal information on the following legal bases: your consent, performance of a
        contract with you, our legitimate interests in operating and securing our business, and
        compliance with legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the following rights:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>CCPA (California):</strong> right to know, right to delete, right to correct, right to opt out of sale or sharing, right to limit use of sensitive personal information, and right to non-discrimination.</li>
        <li><strong>GDPR (EEA and UK):</strong> right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability, and objection.</li>
        <li><strong>PIPEDA (Canada):</strong> right to access your personal information, right to challenge accuracy, and right to withdraw consent subject to legal and contractual restrictions.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We will respond within the timeframe
        required by applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use essential cookies to operate the site and may use analytics tools to understand
        site usage. Where required by law, we obtain consent before placing non-essential cookies
        or analytics tags. You can control cookies through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain personal information for as long as needed to provide our services, comply with
        legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements. Retention periods vary
        by data type and are reviewed periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect personal
        information against unauthorized access, use, disclosure, alteration, or destruction.
        Our managed services posture is ISO 27001 aligned through the Technology Assurance Group
        network. Fortify AI deployments operate inside an environment underwritten by Lloyd&rsquo;s
        of London cybersecurity insurance policy.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Information may be stored and processed in the United States or other jurisdictions. We
        use appropriate safeguards, including contractual measures, where required by applicable
        law.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the &ldquo;Last
        updated&rdquo; date above. Material changes will be communicated as required by applicable
        law.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or your information can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="disclaimer">
        This privacy policy is informational and is not legal advice. If you require legal advice
        about how this policy applies to your situation, consult qualified counsel.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .legal h2 { margin-top: var(--space-7); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .legal h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal ul { display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .legal p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
</style>
